WEBVTT

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.788
and those bills fail,
because the public was well-informed.

00:06:31.812 --> 00:06:33.757
Readers go to the polls

00:06:33.781 --> 00:06:37.314
and they know the pros and cons
behind every ballot measure,

00:06:37.338 --> 00:06:40.290
because journalists
did the heavy lifting for them.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.925
Even better,

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:44.958
researchers have found
that reading a local paper

00:06:44.982 --> 00:06:49.682
can mobilize 13 percent
of nonvoters to vote.

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:51.513
Thirteen percent.

00:06:51.537 --> 00:06:56.601
(Applause)

00:06:56.625 --> 00:07:00.426
That's the number that can change
the outcome of many elections.